      ],
      "updated": 1788934186358,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--> Run time error is called exception .\n\nWhat java does by default when exception occurs ?\n\n1. immedeatly kills the programme .\n\n2. Describe the exception but in very technical manner .\n\nSo , by exception handling we can overcome these behaviour \nexception handling benefits \n\n1. not killing programme \n2. displaying error messages in easy to to understand way .\n\n--> So exception handling makes our programme strong and user friendly .\n\n\nException handling provides us 5 keywords\n=======================================\n\n1. try\n2. catch\n3. throw\n4. throws\n5. finally\n\nSynatx\n======\n\ntry{\n.........\n.............\n..........\n} \ncatch(<Exception_class> <ref>) {\n............ \n  }",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> Run time error is called exception .\n\nWhat java does by default when exception occurs ?\n\n1. immedeatly kills the programme .\n\n2. Describe the exception but in very technical manner .\n\nSo , by exception handling we can overcome these behaviour \nexception handling benefits \n\n1. not killing programme \n2. displaying error messages in easy to to understand way .\n\n--> So exception handling makes our programme strong and user friendly .\n\n\nException handling provides us 5 keywords\n=======================================\n\n1. try\n2. catch\n3. throw\n4. throws\n5. finally\n\nSynatx\n======\n\ntry{\n.........\n.............\n..........\n} \ncatch(<Exception_class> <ref>) {\n............ \n  }",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
