    {
      "id": "z4AU-sX_uC-Dxmzua0INi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 253,
      "y": 1153,
      "width": 547,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 466761313,
      "version": 917,
      "versionNonce": 1033694369,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788934621749,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "### Rule 1\n\nWhenever an exception occurs inside the `try` block at\nany line, Java **immediately stops executing the\nremaining statements of that `try` block**.\n\n### Rule 2\n\nWhen an exception occurs, Java creates/throws an\n**exception object** representing the type of\nexception that occurred.\n\nJava then searches for a **matching `catch` block\nfrom top to bottom**.\n\nThe first compatible `catch` block is executed.\n\nAfter the `catch` block finishes, the program\ncontinues executing the **code after the try-catch\nstatement**.\n\nThis way, the exception can be handled instead of\ncausing immediate program termination.\n\nIf no matching `catch` block is found, the exception\nbecomes **uncaught**, and the current thread\nterminates.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "### Rule 1\n\nWhenever an exception occurs inside the `try` block at any line, Java **immediately stops executing the remaining statements of that `try` block**.\n\n### Rule 2\n\nWhen an exception occurs, Java creates/throws an **exception object** representing the type of exception that occurred.\n\nJava then searches for a **matching `catch` block from top to bottom**.\n\nThe first compatible `catch` block is executed.\n\nAfter the `catch` block finishes, the program continues executing the **code after the try-catch statement**.\n\nThis way, the exception can be handled instead of causing immediate program termination.\n\nIf no matching `catch` block is found, the exception becomes **uncaught**, and the current thread terminates.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
